;Oden::DSKG:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1986-11-22 23:03:35, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;202	You cannot ask the high segment for its start address because it's
;	concealed from the low segment, and the GETSEG UUO clears the low
;	segment start address .JBSA, so, the entry vector must	be the first
;	thing in the high segment if you are to be able to JRST there from
;	the low segment.
;	The GETSEG UUO also makes life hard it other ways:
;	(1)	put REENTER address for high segment in high segment, so we
;		can put it into .JBREN for REENTER command
;	(2)	copy .JBSA from .JBHSA for START command (only RH)
;	(3)	put version# in high segment, so we can put it into .JBVER
;	(4)	the segment name is not the same as the program name (we must
