;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-06-11 14:03:14, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;64	Moved TOPS-20 JSYS error hacking to QUIT, and constants to KOMMAC.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-05-28 15:58:25, Edit by THOLERUS T
;63	Added dirty hack in GFRESH in module DBPRO.  Version 6B(7)-3.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-05-21 10:42:22, Edit by THOLERUS T
;62	Corrected bug in FINDBL in module FIND.  Version 6B(6)-3.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-05-08 12:47:07, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;61	Make LMENU understand short menus. This is now version 6B(5)-3.
;	Make cost output routine be more specific about errors.
;	Unmake edit #51, since it might give problems. (Note: KOM-20 has no
;	such feature yet.)
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-05-02 16:11:58, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;60	Version 6B(3): protected names improved.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-04-30 19:32:31, Edit by KPJ @ NADJA
;57	Use standard DIGITAL format of version word.
;	This is now version 6B(1).
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-04-22 23:43:37, Edit by KPJ @ NADJA
;56	VIEWDATA support code added.
;Freja::Ps:<KOM.6-SOURCES>MONITO.MAC.13 20-Apr-85 01:19:36,Editor:KPJ-JAAKKOLA
;55	Implemented new fascist code to test for various nasty conditions which
;	makes us barf:
;		switches off UUO simulation on TOPS-20 for security reasons
;		(KL10) non-zero section not supported by us
;		need ^C capability on TOPS-20
;		refuses to go on after being stopped with ^C
;Freja::Ps:<KOM.6-SOURCES>MONITO.MAC.10 18-Apr-85 19:13:05,Editor:KPJ-JAAKKOLA
;54	Tops-10 LMENU TMPCOR file is now TMP:LME (was TMP:KJO). The contents
;	have changed to the new format understood by LMENU.
;Freja::Ps:<KOM.6-SOURCES>MONITO.MAC.7 18-Apr-85 14:32:07,Editor:KPJ-JAAKKOLA
;53	Fix bug in controlling TTY handling.
;Freja::Ps:<Kom.6-Sources>Monito.Mac.2 11-Apr-85 17:12:48,Editor:KPJ-Jaakkola
;52	Flag HAVENQ now *really* used on TOPS-20 too.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-04-11 14:25:16, Edit by KPJ @ PCOM
;51	Since KOM-10 wakes up once in a while (currently 60s), there is no
;	reason to return to monitor after a timeout.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-04-10 12:28:01, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;50	Version changed to 6A(1024)-3 by request from Sven Olofsson QZ.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-03-28 12:30:59, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;47	Symbol to point at version word. Use standard TOPS-20 symbols for
;	version word fields. This is now version 6A(1024)-6. Changed PRCIN3
;	to suppress trailing spaces.
;Freja::<KOM.6-SOURCES>MONITO.MAC.3 15-Mar-85 02:44:18,Editor:KPJ-JAAKKOLA
;46	Zero name on TOPS-20 is called "(priv)" by default.
;	Flag HAVENQ now used on TOPS-20 too.
;	Same handling of ^C on data base lock on both systems (protects
;	against database crash due to user ^C)
;	Same handling of ^C on password input on both systems.
;	Correct sense of FTPHON usage.
;	Use standard "local labels" syntax.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-03-21 10:38:40, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;45	Load ERRLOG module only when error logging enabled.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-03-13 23:21:11, Edit by KPJ @ AIDA
;44	Make this version 1024.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC<62,7777,MAC> 1985-03-13 22:01:49, Edit by KPJ @ AIDA
;43	Make program understand process controlling terminal concept.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-03-08 03:04:54, Edit by KPJ @ NADJA
;42	Get rid of QACR calls. Fixed bug in SETACR which made personal flag
;	AUTOMATIC fail at times.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-03-04 17:17:03, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;41	Make all "impossible" error returns give a warning (expect when
;	DETACHed). Try to dequeue database if we have a resource or waiting
;	for resource.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-03-01 16:58:53, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;40	"Text phones" now under switch FTPHON. Sanitized code.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-02-26 07:54:55, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;37	Moved magical numbers to KOMMAC. Fixed bug in cost output routine.
;	Routine to test if Tops-10 SFDs feature exists on system, and how
;	deep they are allowed to nest. New routine CHKTTY to set terminal
;	type dependent things.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-02-26 07:13:54, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;36	MACRO-10 bug with literals generates lots of Phase-errors, and
;	LINK-10 crashes with illegal memory reference. Trying code reformatting
;	to sidestep this.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777,MAC] 1985-02-25 14:01:31, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;35	Use standard character names. Moved local macros to KOMMAC.
;	Get rid of useless TRMOP.-macros. Restore ACR and TTY CRLF settings
;	when halting.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1985-01-30 13:29:35, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;34	Problems with LF here and there. KOM must be fixed to trig on LF
;	instead of CR. Till that have been done, on Tops-10 edit 33 is off.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1985-01-16 05:40:16, Edit by KPJ @ GRAV
;33	Allow LF to end commands.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1985-01-14 00:36:47, Edit by KPJ @ AIDA
;32	Check if the EXEC fork is still with us, and create it if it is lost.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1985-01-07 20:45:01, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;31	Make personal flag DISCONNECT AFTER LOGOUT work on TOPS-20 too.
;	Got rid of crummy QDISCO routine. Rewrote ECHOFF/SEECOF routine.
;	ECHFLG only used here, localized. Got rid of QLFECH calls.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-12-24 16:03:57, Edit by KPJ @ AIDA
;30	Stop fiddling with MIC echo. Got rid of TMPFLG, which is not used.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-12-11 06:49:31, Edit by KPJ @ NADJA
;27	RUNX literals must be in low segment, since RUNX zaps away the hiseg.
;Freja::<Kom.6-Sources>Monito.Mac.2 10-Dec-84 15:09:25,Editor:KPJ-Jaakkola
;26	Misspelling in T20 code (".CNCNZ" == ".CHCNZ")
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-12-04 21:43:50, Edit by KPJ @ NADJA
;25	Implement T10 LOGOUT command to care about DISCONNECT flag.
;	QZ-special hacking for FOA persons: FOA-PPN ==> logout always!
;24	(this space intentionally left blank)
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-12-03 16:46:32, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;23	We are now running [edit 1023]. Hurray!
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-12-03 13:28:11, Edit by KPJ @ L89
;22	New routine to write a TMP:KJO file. It contains "K/C" when
;	personal flag DISCONNECT AFTER LOGOUT is OFF. Called from QUIT.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-29 02:58:27, Edit by KPJ @ UPSALA
;21	Make a SESSION cost output routine.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-23 11:37:34, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;20	Obey the line width as given, and don't assume wrapping column.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-19 18:25:05, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;17	Made reference to TEXTER module.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-19 11:00:41, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;16	Refer to RUNTAB only when CALL commands active.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-12 19:30:29, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;15	LOGOUT routine incorporated.,
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-12 12:53:11, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;14	Now the ^C routine is called TRPSTP on both T10 and T20 (was called
;	CCINT on T20). Deleted inaccessible code in T10 TRPSTP. Set flag
;	STPFLG, when ^C succeeds, which is checked in QUIT.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-11-02 09:53:54, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;13	Moved magical numbers to KOMMAT.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-10-12 15:31:24, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;12	COPYRIGHT is not used anywhere. Deleted. Inserted COPYRIGHT macro.
;	Globals not used except in this module: DETFLG - localized.
;Oden::DSKD:MONITO.MAC[62,7777] 1984-10-04 05:30:38, Edit by K.JAAKKOLA
;11	Cleanup code for future changes.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-09-25 02:12:43, Edit by K.Jaakkola
;10	Inserted (c) message as an ASCIZ string in the code.
;	Deleted KSYWRN variable. Documented buffer control block, version
;	word and 20x entry vector for future generations.
;	ENQWAT and HAVENQ not global anymore.
;	UMODF (T20) deleted, since it was PC%USR really.
;	STPFLG is never changed on Tops-10. Put into T20 conditional.
;	RSET routine does nothing under TOPS-20. Put into T10 conditional.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-09-19 18:12:35, Edit by K.Jaakkola
;7	Problem with RUNX at TOPS-20 fixed.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-09-17 20:19:08, Edit by K.Jaakkola
;6	Included BCQs TOPS-20 hacks:
;;;	;Freja::QS:<BJORN-CARLSSON.KOM-LOGIN>MONITO.MAC.2, 10-Sep-84 17:03:33,
;;;							 Ed: BJORN-CARLSSON
;;;	;3	Some hacks to allow COM-login.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-09-14 10:08:14, Edit by K.Jaakkola
;5	Moved PAGIN, PAGOUT and PAGDEL under T10-conditional, since memory
;	managing is never necessary under TOPS-20.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-09-14 09:29:47, Edit by K.Jaakkola
;4	Rewrote TOPS-20 RUNFRK routine to not crash for everything. It will
;	now instead say what went wrong, and return failure.
;	This also is a temporary fix to these errors:
;	known bug #8	if you reset your editor fork outside KOM,
;			you got "runfrk (sfrkv)" crash, with JSYS error
;			"Invalid process handle". Now you will not crash.
;	known bug #29	if you reset your EXEC fork outside KOM,
;			you got "runfrk (sfrkv)" crash, with JSYS error
;			"Invalid process handle". Now you will not crash.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-09-04 06:15:46, Edit by K.Jaakkola
;3	Somebody had hacked this module so MACRO barfed over it.
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-06-25 15:57:59, Edit by KPJ Jaakkola
;2	^G interrupt routine fixed to not crash KOM with "inblk monfil"
;	(known bug #14)
;Oden::Dskd:Monito.Mac[62,7777] 1984-05-23 05:39:15, Edit by KPJ Jaakkola
;1	Merged T20 and T10 versions. Updated to version 1017: new version,
;	.UNDO is no longer with us, text phone hacking incorporated (BCQ
;	hacking...), lots of fancy backspace hacking (BCQ/BDQ), try to
;	disconnect line at times, and one or two more hacks...
;======================================================================

	SEARCH	kommac
	PROLOG	(monito,hisegm)		;<KPJ.115>

;Copyright (c) Swedish National Defense Research Institute
;Copyright (c) QZ Computing Centre, 1984
;Copyright (c) QZ Computing Centre, 1987

	kommaj==6		;major version
	kommin==3		;minor version
	komedt==editnr		;edit#
	komwho==0		;last hacker (well, not quite OK, but...)

				;Version number:

		;   0   2 3	 12 13	      17 18			 35
		;  +=====+=========+============+==========================+
		;  ! who ! version !  minor     !	    edit	   !
		;  +=====+=========+============+==========================+

versio==:FLD(komwho,VI%WHO)!
	 FLD(kommaj,VI%MAJ)!
	 FLD(kommin,VI%MIN)!
	 FLD(komedt,VI%EDN)

T10,<
IFN	<.-hisegm>,<		;<KPJ.202> must be FIRST in the high segment
PRINTX	?Entry vector block is not at high segment start. Moby lossage...
PRINTX	?Must because LOWSEG can't find out start address of concealed HISEG
PRINTX	<Execution suppressed>

evec::	PORTAL	crashj		;START address
	PORTAL	crashj		;CCL address
	JRST	crashj		;data base create
	PORTAL	crashj		;segment return
myvers::EXP	versio		;<KPJ.202> version
myree:	EXP	crashj		;<KPJ.202> REENTER address for high segment
crashj:	OUTSTR[	ASCIZ	!
?Compilation error in MONITO - execution fails!]
	EXIT	0,
>;High segment bad
IFE	<.-hisegm>,<
evec::	PORTAL	start##		;/RUNOFFSET:0	normal entry
	PORTAL	cclent##	;/RUNOFFSET:1	CCL entry
	JRST	create##	;/RUNOFFSET:2	create data base
	PORTAL	segret		;/RUNOFFSET:3	segment return
myvers::EXP	versio		;<KPJ.202> version
myree:	EXP	reent##		;<KPJ.202> REENTER address for high segment
>;High segment OK
>;T10
T20,<				;	TOPS-20 entry vector	<KPJ.103>
				; +=====================================+
evec::	JRST	start##		; !	      START address		!
				; +=====================================+
	JRST	cclent##	; !	    REENTER address		!
				; +=====================================+
myvers::EXP	versio		; !<KPJ.47>    version number		!
				; +=====================================+
	JRST	create##	; !	   entry to create data base	!
				; +=====================================+
	evclen==.-evec		;<KPJ.146>
>;T20	

;	E X T E R N A L S

T10,<	EXTERN	ptykom>
	EXTERN	exclud,prior,nexcom
	EXTERN	uppmun,waitx,monfil,montmp,dbpro,defspe,revfun
	EXTERN	rdobj,loaemp,creemp
	EXTERN	movent,deamon,delobj
	EXTERN	outent,prirec,mark,cremar,revtab,chkrec,chanam
	EXTERN	subtra,updlse,help,alltab,chatab,chapre
	EXTERN	calvid,chatyp,search,add,prpest
	EXTERN	onlyre,site,member,creloc,gtname,chknew,zapobj
	EXTERN	rdnext,joinmt,lismee,cremee,creatm,crepre
	EXTERN	lispre,nexlet,mkmess,mkcomm,review,displa
	EXTERN	addlnk,crelnk,addent,dbcon,oerase,tertab
	EXTERN	objsta,sysinf,lisper,reptim,liscom
	EXTERN	creper,crenam,mkmenu,chapgs,wrient,writee
	EXTERN	entcon,adreli,filpro,filcon,refina,prnews
	EXTERN	edit,enter,addlis,login,newnam,getnum
IFN	ftcomp,<EXTERN	comput>
	EXTERN	strcon,match,getchr,read,topcom,terpro ;<KPJ.162>
	EXTERN	tercon,strpro,find,updbeg,quit,genera,new
	EXTERN	scndat,texter
	EXTERN	errlog
RUNIF,<	EXTERN	runtab>			;<KPJ.172> only if CALL commands

T10,<					;[KPJ.35]
;T1, T2, T3, T4 must be in that order for this module to work.

IFN	<<t2-t1>-1>,<PRINTX ? T1 and T2 not in order.>
IFN	<<t3-t2>-1>,<PRINTX ? T2 and T3 not in order.>
IFN	<<t4-t3>-1>,<PRINTX ? T3 and T4 not in order.>
>;T10



T10,<				;never written into, put into high segment
;-----------------------------------
;+
;TTYCON		Output done on TTY channel done interrupt (Tops-10)
;-

ttycon::EXP	ttycha				;channel number
	XWD	<psiout##-psivec##>,PS.ROD	;vector offset,,reason
						;reason = output done
	XWD	0,0				;priority,,0
;-----------------------------------
;+
;DATCON		ATTACH/DETACH interrupt condition (Tops-10)
;-

datcon:	.PCDAT					;ATTACH/DETACH call executed
	XWD	<psidat##-psivec##>,0		;vector offset,,reasons
	XWD	2,0				;priority,,0
;-----------------------------------
;+
;STPCON		^C interrupt
;-

stpcon:	.PCSTP					;^C intercept
	XWD	<psistp##-psivec##>,0		;vector offset,,reasons
	XWD	1,0				;priority,,0
;-----------------------------------
;+
;TLECON		Time limit exceeded interrupt condition (Tops-10)
;-

tlecon:	.PCTLE					;time limit exceeded
	XWD	<psitle##-psivec##>,0		;vector offset,,reasons
	XWD	2,0				;priority,,0
;-----------------------------------
;+
;CJICON		Cross-job interrupt interrupt condition (Tops-10)
;-

cjicon:	.PCJBI					;crossjob interrupt
	XWD	<psicji##-psivec##>,0		;vector offset,,reasons
	XWD	2,0				;priority,,0
;-----------------------------------
;+
;QUECON		ENQ resource free interrupt condition (Tops-10)
;-

quecon:	.PCQUE					;<TEQ> ENQ resource available
	XWD	<psique##-psivec##>,0		;<TEQ> vector offset,,reasons
	XWD	2,0				;<TEQ> priority,,0
>;T10
T20,<					;level table
levtab:	lev1pc##			;1	^C
	lev2pc##			;2	^T, ^A, ^O, normal input
	lev3pc##			;3	(unused)

				;never written into, write-protect

chntab:	channel	cc.chn,1,trpstp		;0	^C intercept, priority 1
	channel	typchn,2,ttyint		;1	character typed,priority 2
REPEAT	0,<channel	cg.chn,2,cgint>	;2	^G-interrupt, priority 2
REPEAT	1,<0>				;	no ^G interrupt
	channel	ca.chn,2,caint		;3	^A-interrupt, priority 2
	channel	co.chn,2,coint		;4	^O-interrupt, priority 2
	BLOCK	^D36-<.-chntab>		;the rest is unused
>;T20
T10,<				;T10 ENQ/DEQ block never written into, hi seg
enqblk:	FLD(0,^O77B5)!FLD(1,^O7777B17)!FLD(enqlen,^O777777)
					;size, number, length
	0,,0				;0,,request identifier
	FLD(0,^O37777B17)!FLD(cencha,^O777777)
					;level#,,channel#
	<^O500000+0>,,0			;500000+user code,,0
	0,,0				;size of pool,,number requested
enqlen==.-enqblk
>;T10

	ASCIZ	"
Copyright (c) 1984,1985,1987
		   by   Stockholm University Computing Center, QZ,
			Box 27322, S-102 54 Stockholm, SWEDEN.

This  software is furnished under a license and may be used and copied
only  in  accordance  with  the  terms  of  such  license and with the
inclusion  of  the above copyright notice.  This software or any other
copies  thereof may not be provided or otherwise made available to any
other  person.   No  title  to and ownership of the software is hereby
transferred.   The  information  in this software is subject to change
without  notice  and  should  not  be  construed  as  a  commitment by
the Stockholm University Computing Center, QZ."

;+
;MORDOR		special fascist control code		<KPJ.55>
;		puts up stack pointer.
;called:	JSP	5,mordor
;returns	+1 if all requirements to run program exists
;-

mordor::MOVE	1,[%CNMNT]		;get monitor type
	CALLI	1,^O41			;<KPJ.243> get the information
	 MOVSI	1,(CN%MNX)		;error, treat as unknown monitor type
	TLNE	1,(CN%MNX)		;unknown monitor type?
	 JRST[	JRST	4,^O4711	;<KPJ.243> yes, halt
		JRST	mordor]		;<KPJ.243> continue
	AND	1,[CN%MNT]		;extract monitor type
					;now, see if stupid mistake here...
T10,<	CAMN	1,[FLD(.CNT20,CN%MNT)]>	;Tops-10 code on TOPS-20 ?
T20,<	CAMN	1,[FLD(.CNT10,CN%MNT)]>	;TOPS-20 code on Tops-10 ?
	 JRST[				;yes, someone goofed
T10,<		HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !Cannot run Tops-10 code on TOPS-20!]
		JSYS	^O313		;<KPJ.242> yell a bit
		JSYS	^O170		;<KPJ.242> die
>;T10
T20,<		TTCALL	3,[ASCIZ !?
Cannot run TOPS-20 code on Tops-10!]	;<KPJ.243> OUTSTR
		CALLI	1,^O12		;<KPJ.243> EXIT to monitor				
>;T20
		JRST	.]		;don't allow CONTINUE
					;now see if any unsupported monitor..
T10,<	CAME	1,[FLD(.CNT10,CN%MNT)]>	;Tops-10?
T20,<	CAME	1,[FLD(.CNT20,CN%MNT)]>	;TOPS-20?
	 JRST[	JRST	4,^O666		;<KPJ.242> no, unsupported monitor
		JRST	.]		;refuse continue

;	- - - - - - - - - - - -

T20,<
mordo5:	$Dmovi	1,.FHSLF,<-1>		;<KPJ.245>
	SCVEC%				;do it
	ERJMP[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !Cannot disable UUO simulation:!]
		ESOUT%			;<KPJ.245>
		HALTF%			;<KPJ.245>
		JSR	4,.erstr	;<KPJ.245>
		HALTF%			;<KPJ.245>
		JRST	mordo5]		;<KPJ.245> try again
>;T20
	$Setz	1,			;<KPJ.245!KPJ.201> clear old contents
	XHLLI	1,mordor		;get section# (or 0) into LH
	JUMPN	1,[			;using extended addressing?
T10,<		OUTSTR[	ASCIZ !?Cannot run in non-zero section!]
		EXIT	0,		;die hard
>;T10
T20,<		HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !Cannot run in non-zero section!]
mordo1:		ESOUT%			;say we don't like it
		HALTF%			;return to superior
		HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !Cannot CONTINUE - GET into zero section!]
		JRST	mordo1		;no CONTINUE
>;T20
		]			;end of non-zero section test

;	- - - - - - - - - - - - -

T20,<
mordo4:	$Dmovi	1,0,<-1,,4>		;<KPJ.245> this job, one word into AC4
	MOVEI	3,.JIBAT		;batch controlled? flag
	GETJI%				;obtain info about us
	 ERJMP[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !GETJI failure - !]
		ESOUT%			;<KPJ.245>
		JSR	4,.erstr	;<KPJ.245> display latest error code
		HALTF%			;<KPJ.245>
		JRST	mordo4]		;<KPJ.245> try again
	MOVEM	4,batchf##		;save batch flag
	MOVEI	1,.FHSLF		;this fork
	RPCAP%				;get our capabilities
	ERJMP[	JSR	4,.erstr	;<KPJ.245> ugh
		HALTF%			;<KPJ.245> thud
		JRST	mordo4]		;<KPJ.245> try again
	TLO	3,(SC%CTC)		;enable ^C capability
	EPCAP%				;set the new capabilities
	ERJMP[	JSR	4,.erstr	;<KPJ.245> ouch
		HALTF%			;<KPJ.245> pow
		JRST	mordo4]		;<KPJ.245> try again
	RPCAP%				;get the capabilities again
	ERJMP[	JSR	4,.erstr	;<KPJ.245> argh
		HALTF%			;<KPJ.245> zonk
		JRST	mordo4]		;<KPJ.245> try again
	TLNN	3,(SC%CTC)		;well, do we have the ^C capability?
	 JUMPE	4,[			;<KPJ.225> and not a batch job?
		HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !Need Control-C capability to run program!]
		ESOUT%			;tell user we like ^C capability
		HALTF%			;die
		JRST	mordo4]		;<KPJ.245> try again
>;T20

mordo3:	SKIPE	stpflg##		;stopped by ^C lately?
	 JRST[	$Psout	zctrlc##	;<KPJ.245> yes, we have objections
		$Exit			;<KPJ.245> die
		JRST	mordo3]		;<KPJ.245> one more

T10,<	SKIPE	xmyslf##		;<KPJ.210> have initialized the world?
	 JRST	mordo9			;<KPJ.210> yep, exit
	SETOM	samnes##		;<KPJ.210> we are a virgin high segment
	HRROI	t,.GTRDV		;<KPJ.210> get "run device"
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.210> . . .
	 JRST	mordo8			;<KPJ.210> failed, give up
	MOVEM	t,xmyslf##+0		;<KPJ.210> save away our name
	HRROI	t,.GTRFN		;<KPJ.210> get "run file name"
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.210> . . .
	 JRST	mordo8			;<KPJ.210> failed, give up
	MOVEM	t,xmyslf##+1		;<KPJ.210> save away our name
	SETZM	xmyslf##+2		;<KPJ.210> extension unknown
	SETZM	xmyslf##+3		;<KPJ.210> always zero
	MOVEI	t,xmypth##		;<KPJ.143> path block address
	MOVEM	t,xmyslf##+4		;<KPJ.143> store in GETSEG block
	HRROI	t,.GTRDI		;<KPJ.210> get "run directory"
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.210> . . .
	 JRST	mordo8			;<KPJ.210> failed, give up
	MOVEM	t,xmypth##+2		;<KPJ.210> save PPN
	SETZM	xmypth##+3		;<KPJ.210> zero away SFD list
	MOVE	t,[%FTSTR]		;<KPJ.210> get feature word
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.210> . . .
	 JRST	mordo8			;<KPJ.210> failed, give up
	TRNN	t,<F%SFD&^O777777>	;<KPJ.210> monitor likes SFDs?
	 JRST	mordo9			;<KPJ.210> no, we are done
	MOVE	t,[%LDSFD]		;<KPJ.210> get max #SFDs
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.210>
	 JRST	mordo8			;<KPJ.210> failed, give up
	MOVN	t2,t			;<KPJ.210> make negative counter
	HRLZ	t2,t2			;<KPJ.210> -nn,,0
mordo7:	HRROI	t,.GTRS0(t2)		;<KPJ.210> get "run SFD name"
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.210> . . .
	 JRST	mordo8			;<KPJ.210> failed, give up
	MOVEM	t,xmypth##+3(t2)	;<KPJ.210> save in SFD list
	JUMPE	t,mordo9		;<KPJ.210> end of list?
	AOBJN	t2,mordo7		;<KPJ.210> get next name in list
	$Skipa				;<KPJ.210> done
mordo8:	 SETOM	xmyslf##+0		;<KPJ.210> we don't our high seg. name
mordo9:					;<KPJ.210>
>;T10
	JRST	0(5)			;return to caller


;+
T20,<					;<KPJ.245> MORDOR subroutine
;.ERSTR		special subroutine for MORDOR
;		used to output latest error code for this fork
;call:		JSR	4,.erstr
;returns	+1 always
;-

.erstr:	$Dmovi	1,.PRIOUT,<.FHSLF,,-1>	;<KPJ.245>
	$Setz	3,			;<KPJ.245>
	ERSTR%				;<KPJ.245>
	 ERJMP[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !(internal error 1 in ERSTR)!]
		PSOUT%			;<KPJ.245>
		JRST	0(4)]		;<KPJ.245>
	 ERJMP[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !(internal error 2 in ERSTR)!]
		PSOUT%			;<KPJ.245>
		JRST	0(4)]		;<KPJ.245>
	JRST	0(4)			;<KPJ.245>
>;T20

;+
;INITTY		initialize terminal
;-

initty::save	<nr>
T10,<	$Crlf>				;<KPJ.133!KPJ.111> go to at left margin
	SETZM	linpos##		;initialize line position
T10,<	HRRZ	t,.JBREL		;<KPJ.204> initialize end-of-lowseg
	MOVEM	t,.JBFF			;...from .JBREL
	GETPPN	t,			;get own PPN
	 Nop
>;T10
T20,<
initt1:	MOVEI	1,.FHSLF		;<KPJ.43> this fork
	SCTTY%				;<KPJ.43> get controlling terminal
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> thud
	CAIN	2,.CTTRM		;<KPJ.53> job controlling terminal?
	 JRST[	GJINF%			;<KPJ.43> yes, what is it?
		MOVE	2,4		;<KPJ.43> return it
		JRST	.+1]		;<KPJ.43>
	JUMPL	2,[
		MOVEI	1,.CHSPC	;<KPJ.201!KPJ.43!BDQ> if detached,
		PBOUT%			;[BDQ] block in output wait
		JRST	initt1]		;<KPJ.43!BDQ> until reattached
	GJINF%				;<KPJ.53> get our user#
>;T20
	MOVEM	t,selfpp##		;save it
	CALL	reitty			;reinitialize terminal
T10,<	SETOM	echflg##		;set echo flag on
	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
IFE	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> even more using?
	$Dmovi	t,<2,,t2>,.TOLCP	;<KPJ.245> yep
>;t2=t+1
IFN	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> nope
	$Movx	t,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
	MOVEI	t2,.TOLCP		;<KPJ.35> read "local copy" (echo)
>;t2<>t+1
>;can use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
IFE	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> might?
	$Dmovi	t,<2,,trmblk##>,.TOLCP	;<KPJ.245> yep
>;t2=t+1
IFN	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> might not?
	MOVE	t,[2,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> nope
	MOVEI	t2,TOLCP		;<KPJ.245> read "local copy" (echo)
>;t2<>t+1
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.35>
	 nop
	SKIPLE	t			;echo on ?
	 SETZM	echflg##		;no
>;T10
	CALL	chktty			;<KPJ.37> get terminal data

T10,<	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs?
IFE	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> even more?
	$Dmovi	t,<2,,t2>,.TOLCT	;<KPJ.245> yep
>;t2=t+1
IFN	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> not even more?
	$Movx	t,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> len,,addr
	MOVEI	t2,.TOLCT		;<KPJ.35> get "lowercase bit"
>;t2#t+1
>;can use ACs
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEI	t2,.TOLCT		;<KPJ.35> get "lowercase bit"
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[2,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito initty trmop read tolct>
	MOVEM	t,trmlct##		;<KPJ.35> save away old LC value

	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
IFN	<t4-t3-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
IFE	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> even more?
	$Dmovi	t,<3,,t2>,.TOLCT+.TOSET	;<KPJ.245> yep
>;t2=t+1
IFN	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> not even more?
	$Movx	t,<3,,t2>		;<KPJ.245> nope
	MOVEI	t2,.TOLCT+.TOSET	;<KPJ.35> set lower case
>;t2<>t+1
	$Setz	t4,			;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> lower case ON, please
>;can use ACs
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEI	t2,.TOLCT+.TOSET	;<KPJ.245> set lower case
KL10,<	IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<		;<KPJ.245> hm?
	DMOVE	t2,trmblk##		;<KPJ.245> yep
>;t3=t2+1
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> sob
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
>>;KL10
KL10N,<	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
>;KL10N
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
	SETZM	trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.245> lower case ON, please
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.35> set lower case
	 warn	<monito initty trmop write tolct>

	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs?
IFE	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> even more?
	$Dmovi	t,<2,,t2>,.TOFNC	;<KPJ.245> yep
>;t2=t+1
IFN	<t2-t-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> not even more?
	$Movx	t,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> len,,addr
	MOVEI	t2,.TONFC		;<KPJ.35> get "CR/LF bit"
>;t2<>t+1
>;can use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEI	t2,.TONFC		;<KPJ.35> get "CR/LF bit"
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[2,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito initty trmop read tonfc>
	MOVEM	t,trmnfc##		;<KPJ.35> save old value
	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
	MOVEI	t2,.TONFC+.TOSET	;<KPJ.35> CRLF bit
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
	MOVEI	t4,1			;<KPJ.35> set NO CRLF
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	t,<3,,t2>		;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;can use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEM	t4,trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito initty trmop write tonfc>

	MOVEI	t2,.TOLNB		;<KPJ.135> get "TTY LENGTH nn"
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.135!KPJ.35> controlling TTY
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can se ACs
	$Movx	t,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.135!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[2,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;t3<>t2+1
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.135!KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito ttypgs trmop read topsz> ;<KPJ.135!KPJ.41>
	MOVEM	t,oldpsz##		;<KPJ.135!BCQ> save the size

	MOVEI	t2,.TOPSZ		;<KPJ.135> get "TTY PAGE nn"
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.135!KPJ.35> controlling TTY
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	t,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.135!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[2,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;t3<>t2+1
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.135!KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito ttypgs trmop read topsz> ;<KPJ.135!KPJ.41>
	MOVEM	t,oldpag##		;<KPJ.135!BCQ> save the size
>;T10
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;get old settings
	RFMOD%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVEM	2,oldmod##		;save old settings

	TRZ	2,TT%ECM!TT%DAM		;<KPJ.201!BDQ> deferred echo,data mode
	TDO	2,[TT%LCA!FLD(.TTASC,TT%DAM)]
					;<KPJ.245!BDQ> LC, xlate echo/output
	SFMOD%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	STPAR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>

	MOVEI	2,.MORXO		;<BDQ> read PAUSE END-OF-PAGE status
	MTOPR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVEM	3,oldpag##		;<KPJ.135!BDQ> save it

	$Dmovi	2,.MOXOF,.MOOFF		;<KPJ.245!BDQ> then turn it off
	MTOPR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>

	RFCOC%				;get CCOC words
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>

	$Dmovm	2,oldcoc##		;<KPJ.252!KPJ.201!KPJ.134!BDQ> save'm

	TDZ	2,[BYTE(2) 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,0,3,0,3,3,0,0,0,0]	;modify it
	TDO	2,[BYTE(2) 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,2,0,3,0,0,2,0,0,0,0]
			;; @ A B C D E F G H I J K L M N O P Q
	TDZ	3,[BYTE(2) 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,3,3,0,0,0,3]
	TDO	3,[BYTE(2) 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,1,3,0,0,0,3]	;(trick -- simulate)
			;; R S T U V W X Y Z [ \ ] ^ _
	SFCOC%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>

	MOVEI	1,.FHJOB		;get job terminal interrupt word
	RTIW%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVEM	2,oldtiw##		;<BDQ> save it

	TDO	2,[1B<.TICCC>!1B<.TICCO>!1B<.TICCT>! 
		   1B<.TICTI>!1B<.TICCG>!1B<.TICCA>]
	STIW%				;interrupt on ^C,^O,^T,^G,^A
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> what's up, Doc?
	MOVE	t,[POINT 7,rtybuf##,6]	;set up this pointer correctly
	MOVEM	t,rtypnt##
>;T20
	SKIPE	papflg##		;prints on paper?
	 JRST[	MOVEI	t,opgsz2-1	;[KPJ.13] yes, get paper size
		MOVEM	t,maxlin##	;[KPJ.13] set page size
		SETZM	scrfl##		;set scroll flag off
		JRST	.+1]

	CALL	reitty			;one extra open
	CALL	psiini			;go and initialize interrupt system
	return


;+
;CHKTTY	(not documented)
;-

chktty::SETOM	papflg##		;set paper flag on
	SETOM	scrfl##			;scrolls
T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TODIS		;<KPJ.35> read "display" bit
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	MOVE	nr,[2,,t2]		;<KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	nr,[2,,trmblk##]	;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;t3<>t2+1
	TRMOP.	nr,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito chktty read todis>
>;T10
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;get terminal type
	GTTYP%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
KL10,<	ADJBP	2,[POINT 1,trmtps##]>
KL10N,<	PRINTX	?ADJBP in code - you lose (CHKTTY MONITO)
	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !ABJBP in code - you lose (CHKTTY MONITO)!]
	ESOUT%				;<KPJ.245>
	HALTF%				;<KPJ.245>
	MOVE	2,[POINT 1,trmtps##]	;<KPJ.245>
>;KL10N
	ILDB	nr,2			;get display attribute
>;T20
	CAIE	nr,0			;<TEQ> display terminal ?
	 SETZM	papflg##		;yes, no paper then
	CALL	ttywid			;set TTY width

T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOTRM		;<KPJ.35> get SIXBIT terminal type
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	nr,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	nr,[2,,trmblk##]	;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;t3<>t2+1
	TRMOP.	nr,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito chktty trmop read totrm>

IFN	ftphon,<			;<KPJ.40> text phone support?
	CAMN	nr,[SIXBIT !textte!]	;[BCQ] terminal type TEXTTE?
	 CALL	textte##		;[BCQ] yes, set things up
>;ftphon

	CAMN	nr,[SIXBIT !id100!]	; terminal type ID100 ?
	 CALL	termid##		; yes, set colour

IFN	ftview,<			;<KPJ.56> if VIEWDATA support
	CAMN	nr,[SIXBIT !viewda!]	; terminal type VIEWDA ?
	 CALL	termvi##		; yes, set parameters
>;ftview

	SETZM	ansflg##		;clear ANSI flag
	CAME	nr,[SIXBIT !ambass!]	;terminal type AMBASS ?
	 CAMN	nr,[SIXBIT !vt100!]	;or terminal type VT100 ?
	  $Skipa			;yes, set ANSI flag
	   CAMN	nr,[SIXBIT !ansi!]	;terminal type ANSI ?
	    SETOM ansflg##		;yes, set ANSI flag
>;T10
T20,<	SETZM	ansflg##		;clear ANSI flag
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;get terminal type
	GTTYP%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	CAIE	2,.TT102		;<ZOT.247> VT102?
	 CAIN	2,.TT131		;<ZOT.247> or VT131?
	  SETOM	ansflg##		;<ZOT.247> yes, assume ANSI mode
	CAIE	2,^D29			;<KPJ.77> Facit Twist?
	 CAIN	2,.TT100		;is it VT100?
	  SETOM	ansflg##		;yes, assume in ANSI mode
IFN	ftphon,<			;<KPJ.40>
	CAIN	2,.ttext		;<BCQ> Swedish PTT "text phones"?
	 CALL	textte##		;<BCQ> yes, setup for it
>;ftphon
>;T20
	return

;+
;REITTY		reinitialize terminal
;-

reitty::save	<nr>
T10,<	SETZM	detflg##		;we're not detached now!
	SETO	nr,			;our job
	CTLJOB	nr,			;get controlling job number
	 JRST	reitt1			;not implemented, or job number too big
	CAMN	nr,[-1]			;not controlled via a PTY?
	 JRST	reitt1			;no, so use non-blocking I/O
	MOVSI	nr,(UU.AIO)		;get bit to clear
	ANDCAM	nr,opntty##+.OPMOD	;clear "non blocking I/O" bit
reitt1:	OPEN	ttycha,opntty##		;open TTY channel
	 error	<reitty-1 monito>

	PUSH	P,.JBFF			;save old lowseg end

	MOVEI	t,ttibuf##		;we want our own input buffer ring
	MOVEM	t,.JBFF			;tell system where to put it
	INBUF	ttycha,noftti		;TTY channel,,number of buffers

	MOVEI	t,ttobuf##		;we want our own input buffer ring
	MOVEM	t,.JBFF			;tell system where to put it
	OUTBUF	ttycha,noftto		;TTY channel,,number of buffers

	POP	P,.JBFF			;restore old lowseg end
	OUTPUT	ttycha,			;make a dummy OUTPUT
>;T10
T20,<	SETZM	ittbuf##+.BFADR		;<KPJ.201> clear buffer ring header
	SETZM	ittbuf##+.BFPTR		;<KPJ.201>
	SETZM	ittbuf##+.BFCTR		;<KPJ.201>
	MOVEI	t,noftto*^O23*5-1	;max number of characters in buffer
	MOVEM	t,ottbuf##+.BFCTR	;<KPJ.201> setup buffer ring byte count
	MOVE	t,[POINT 7,ttobuf##]	;byte pointer to buffer
	MOVEM	t,ottbuf##+.BFPTR	;<KPJ.201> setup buffer ring byte ptr
>;T20
T10,<	PJOB	nr,			;get job number
	TRMNO.	nr,			;[KPJ.35] get controlling terminal UDX
	 error	<reitty-2 monito>	;couldn't
	MOVEM	nr,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> save UDX
>;T10
	CALL	echon			;echo is on
	return

;+
;SETACR		set ACR
;-

setacr::save	<nr>
T10,<	SKIPN	echflg##		;echo on ?
	 JRST	setac9			;no, forget ACR
>;T10
	MOVE	t,selffl##		;<KPJ.42> get my flags
	Txne	t,acrpfl		;<KPJ.42> any ACR ?
	 JRST	setac1			;yes
	CALL	cleacr			;no, clear ACR
	JRST	setac9

setac1:
T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOACR		;[KPJ.35] get "auto CRLF facility"
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	nr,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;can use Acs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	nr,[2,,trmblk##]	;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	TRMOP.	nr,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito setacr read toacr> ;[KPJ.41]
	MOVEM	nr,trmcr##		;[KPJ.35] save old value

	MOVEI	t2,.TOACR+.TOSET	;[KPJ.35] set ACR flag
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
	MOVEI	t4,irmarg		;<KPJ.42!35> to our inner margin
	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
IFN	<t4-t3-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPj.245> can't
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	t,<3,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;can use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEM	t4,trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito setacr write toacr>
>;T10
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT
	RFMOD%				;<BDQ> check if half-duplex
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVSI	1,(1B0)
	TRNN	2,FLD(.TTHDX&.TTLDX,TT%DUM) ;<BDQ> skip if half-duplex
	 IORM	1,txtbrk##+1		;set bit for wake-up on SPACE
>;T20
setac9:	return


;+
;CLEACR		clear ACR
;-

cleacr::
T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOACR+.TOSET	;<KPJ.35> set ACR
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
	$Setz	t4,			;<KPJ.35> clear ACR
	.foo==0				;<KPJ.245> default can use ACs
IFN	<t4-t3-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.245> can't
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	t,<3,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;can use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEM	t4,trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245>
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito cleacr trmop write toacr>
>;T10
T20,<	MOVSI	t,(1B0)
	ANDCAM	t,txtbrk##+1		;clear bit for wake-up on SPACE
>;T20
	return


;+
;TTYWID		get TTY width
;-

ttywid:	save	<nr>
T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOWID		;<KPJ.35> get "carriage width"
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	nr,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	nr,[2,,trmblk##]	;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
	TRMOP.	nr,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito ttywid trmop read towid> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	$Dmovi	1,.PRIOUT,.MORLW	;<KPJ.246>
	MTOPR%				;read terminal width
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	SKIPN	nr,3
	 MOVEI	nr,infwid		;[BDQ] set infinite width if width=0
>;T20
;;;;	SUBI	nr,1			;[KPJ.20] (don't) adjust for wrap
	MOVEM	nr,crmarg##		;set current right margin
	return


;+
;TTYPGS		get TTY page size  [BDQ & BCQ]
;returns	NR/	crt size,,paper size
;-

ttypgs::
T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOPSZ		;[KPJ.35] get "page setting"
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> controlling TTY
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPj.246> can use ACs
	$Movx	nr,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;can use ACs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.246> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.246> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.246> . . .
	MOVE	nr,[2,,trmblk##]	;<KPJ.246> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	TRMOP.	nr,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito ttypgs trmop read topsz> ;[KPJ.41]

	SKIPN	nr			;[BCQ] if it was set?
	 HLRZ	nr,selfpg##		;[BCQ] wasn't so get number from dbase
	HRLZS	nr			;[BCQ] get it left half
IFN	ftphon,<			;[KPJ.40]
	SKIPE	phone##			;[BCQ] this is a text telephone?
	 HRLI	nr,opgsz3		;[BCQ!KPJ.13] yes, it has 12 lines/page
>;ftphon
	HRR	nr,selfpg##		;[BCQ] get the rigth margin
					;[KPJ.35!KPJ.36!BCQ]
	MOVEI	t2,.TOSET+.TOPSZ	;[KPJ.36] change page size
	SETO	t3,			;[KPJ.36] controlling tty
	SETZ	t4,			;[KPJ.36] reset page mode output
	.foo==0				;<KPJ.246> default can use ACs
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.246> can't
IFN	<t4-t3-1>,<.foo==1>		;<KPJ.246> . . .
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.246> can use ACs
	$Movx	t,<3,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.36> len,,addr
>;can use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.246> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.246> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.246> . . .
	MOVEM	t4,trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.246> . . .
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.246> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.246> forget
	TRMOP.	t,			;[BCQ] reset paged mode output
	 warn	<monito ttypgs trmop write topsz> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	$Dmovi	1,.PRIOUT,.MORLL	;<KPJ.246>
	MTOPR%				;read terminal page length
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	HRRZ	nr,3
	HRL	nr,3
	SKIPE	batchf##
	 HRLI	nr,0			;set screen length 0 if batch job
>;T20
	return




;+
;PSIINI		Initialize the interrupt system
;-

psiini:				;<KPJ.67>
T10,<	MOVEI	t,psivec##
	PIINI.	t,			;initialize the PSI system
	 error	<psiini-1 monito>
					;turn on facility, and add condition
	MOVE	t,[PS.FAC!PS.FON!tlecon] ;"time limit exceeded"
	PISYS.	t,
	 error	<psiini-2 monito>

	MOVE	t,[PS.FAC!ttycon]	;add condition
	PISYS.	t,			; "output done on TTY channel"
	 error	<psiini-3 monito>

	MOVE	t,[PS.FAC!cjicon]	;add condition
	PISYS.	t,			; "crossjob interrupt" (ignore error)
	 warn	<monito psiini pisys psfac>

	MOVE	t,[PS.FAC!datcon]	;Add condition
	PISYS.	t,			; "ATTACH/DETACH call executed"
	 error	<psiini-4 monito>

	MOVE	t,[PS.FAC!quecon]	;<KPJ.127> add condition
	PISYS.	t,			;<KPJ.127> "ENQ got"
	 error	<psiini-5 monito>
>; T10
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.FHSLF
	MOVE	2,[levtab,,chntab]	;level and channel tables
	SIR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	EIR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	SKIPN	batchf##		;<ZOT.244!BDQ> batch has no ^C caps.
	 JRST[	MOVE	1,[.TICCC,,cc.chn] ;assign interrupt on ^C to chan 0
		ATI%
		ERCAL	fatal##		;<KPJ.245>
		JRST	.+1]
	MOVE	1,[.TICTI,,typchn]	; assign interrupt on typein to chan 1
	ATI%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
REPEAT	0,<				;<KPJ.67>
	MOVE	1,[.TICCG,,cg.chn]	; assign interrupt on ^G to chan 2
	ATI%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
>;REPEAT 0				;<KPJ.67>
	MOVE	1,[.TICCA,,ca.chn]	; assign interrupt on ^A to chan 3
	ATI%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVE	1,[.TICCO,,co.chn]	; assign interrupt on ^O to chan 4
	ATI%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVEI	1,.FHSLF
REPEAT	0,<				;<KPJ.67>
	MOVSI	2,(1B<cg.chn>!1B<ca.chn>!1B<co.chn>)
>;REPEAT 0				;<KPJ.67>
REPEAT	1,<
	MOVSI	2,(1B<ca.chn>!1B<co.chn>)
>;REPEAT 1
	AIC%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
>;T20
	return


;+
;PSIOFF		disable interrupt system
;-

psioff::
T10,<	MOVE	t,[PS.FOF!PS.FCP]	;turn off, and clear all pending
	PISYS.	t,
	 warn	<monito psioff pisys>	;don't care, we're leaving anyway
>;T10
T20,<	CIS%				;clear all pending interrupts
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	MOVEI	1,.FHSLF
	DIR%				; disable all interrupts
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
>;T20
	return
	





;+
T10,< ; Twenex can't trap time limit exceeded, and doesn't really need to
      ; either, since a time limit is seldom ever set

;TRPTLE		Here we come, when the users time limit has run out. There
;		really nothing to do about it. Just return from this interrupt
;		and let the user continue running KOM.
;-

trptle::PORTAL	.+1			;<KPJ.213>
	DEBRK.				;dismiss
	 error	<trptle monito>	; shouldn't happen, unless monitor problems!
;	warn	<monito trptle debrk>
	return			; Not at interrupt level?!?! then return
>;T10

;+	
T10,< ; Twenex can't trap ATTACH/DETACH, only carrier drop, and only top fork.

;TRPDAT		Here we arrive when some one has detached or attached
;		us. If we are being DETACHed - set flag to indicate to TTY I/O
;		should be done. If reason is attach, clear this flag
;-

trpdat::PORTAL	.+1			;<KPJ.213>
	save	<t>
	SKIPL	t,psidat##+.PSVIS	;was it an ATTACH?
	 JRST[	SETZM	detflg##	;yes, we are not detached now
		JRST	trpda1]		;<TEQ> restore, return from interrupt
					;*** we are now DETACHed ***
	SETO	t,			;this job
	TRMNO.	t,			;get TTY number
	 TRNA				;failed, we are truly detached
	  JRST[	warn	<monito trpdat trmno>
		JRST	trpda1]		;success, not detached really...
	SETOM	detflg##		;remember we're detached
	SKIPN	havenq##		;if we've resources, ignore interrupt
	 SKIPE	enqwat##		;if waiting for resources, ignore too
	  JRST	trpda1			;yes, ignore interrupt
	SKIPE	sema##			;critical part?
	 JRST	trpda1			;yes, so DON'T sleep!!
	MOVE	t,psidat##+.PSVOP	;get old PC
	HRRZM	t,oldpc##		;and save it
	MOVEI	t,trpda2		;where to "return" after interrupt
	MOVEM	t,psidat##+.PSVOP	;new "old" PC
trpda1:	rstreg				;restore ACs
	DEBRK.				; and dismiss this interrupt
	 error	<trpdat monito>		; failed, should never happen anyway
	warn	<monito trpdat debrk>	;[KPJ.41]

trpda2:	save	<gp1,t>
IFN	ftphon,<			;[KPJ.40]
	SKIPE	phone##			;[BCQ] this is a text hone?
	 JRST	endkom##		;[BCQ] yes, don't wait, logout NOW!
>;ftphon
				;sleep 15 minutes, and check once in a minute
				;for ATTACHed. If still detached after 15
				;minutes, exit

	MOVEI	t,detslp		;[KPJ.37] sleep time at DETACH
trpd10:	MOVEI	gp1,^D60*^D1000*detwak	;[KPJ.37] test interval for ATTACH
	PUSH	P,t			;<KPJ.106> save loop counter
	CALL	sleept			;to sleep
	 nop				;don't care if this fails..
	POP	P,t			;<KPJ.106> restore loop counter
	SKIPE	detflg##		;are we still DETACHed?
	 JRST[	SOJGE	t,trpd10	;yes, we are very tired..
		JRST	endkom##]	;last time, so finish up, and exit
	rstreg				;<KPJ.201> restore stack
	JRST	@oldpc##		;attached, go to where we came from
>;T10



;+
T10,<
;TRPSTP		^C interrupt handler
;		Note: called by interrupt system
;-

trpstp::PORTAL	.+1			;<KPJ.213>
	save	gp1			;<KPJ.67>
	SKIPE	havenq##		;<TEQ> if have resource, ...
	 JRST	trpst9			;[TEQ]    then cannot stop 
	SKIPE	enqwat##		;<TEQ> if something to update, then...
	  JRST	trpst9			;<TEQ> no, hang on for a while more
	MOVEI	gp1,endkom##		;[KPJ.14!TEQ] fake return to stop
	MOVEM	gp1,psistp##+.PSVOP	;<TEQ>
	SETOM	stpflg##		;<KPJ.14> mark we ^C'ed us out...

trpst9:	restore	gp1
	DEBRK.
	 error	<trpstp monito>
	warn	<monito trpstp debrk>
	JRST	endkom##
>;T10


;+
T10,<
;TRPQUE		interrupt for receiving ENQ. lock
;		Note: called by interrupt system
;-

trpque::PORTAL	.+1			;<KPJ.213>
	save	<t>
	SETOM	havenq##		;yes, we are in
	SETZM	enqwat##		;no, no longer waiting
	PJOB	t,
	WAKE	t,		; good morning!
	 warn	<monito trpque wake>
	rstreg			; restore registers
	DEBRK.
	 error	<trpque monito>
	warn	<monito trpque debrk>
	return
>;T10




;+
T10,<
;TRPOUT		TTY output done interrupt
;		Note: called by interrupt system
;-

trpout::PORTAL	.+1			;<KPJ.213>
	SKIPE	enqwat##		;<TEQ> if waiting for ENQ. ...
	 JRST	trpou9			;[TEQ]   then avoid wake
	save	<t>
	PJOB	t,			;[TEQ]
	WAKE	t,			;[TEQ] must wake to avoid race
	 warn	<monito trpout wake>	;[KPJ.41!TEQ] never mind 
	rstreg				;[TEQ]
trpou9:	DEBRK.				; just dismiss the interrupt
	 error	<trpout monito>		; error - DEBRK. failed
	warn	<monito trpout debrk>	;[KPJ.41]
	return				; here if no interrupt in progress
>;T10




;+
;TPUT		just put a character in terminal output buffer
;accepts	CH/	character
;-

tput::
T10,<	SKIPE	detflg##			;we're detached?
	 JRST	tput9				;yes, we can't do any TTY I/O
>;T10
	SOSGE	ottbuf##+.BFCTR			; this buffer full ?
	 JRST	tput2				; yes, flush this, get a new
	IDPB	ch,ottbuf##+.BFPTR		; store character in buffer
T20,<	DPB	ch,rtypnt##			; put the char in ^R-buffer
	$Setz	t,.CHNUL			;[KPJ.13] put a null last..
	IDPB	t,rtypnt##			; ..in the ^R-buffer
	CAIN	ch,.CHLFD			;[KPJ.13] LF ?
	 JRST[	MOVE	t,[POINT 7,rtybuf##,6]	; yes, reset..
		MOVEM	t,rtypnt##		; ..the bytepointer
		$Setz	t,.CHNUL		;[KPJ.13] make ASCIZ
		DPB	t,rtypnt##
		JRST	.+1]
>;T20
	JRST	tput9		; and return

tput2:	CALL	toutpu		; force output buffer to terminal
	JRST	tput		; forced, go and retry

tput9:	return




;+
;TOUTPU		output the terminal buffer
;-

toutpu::
T10,<	SKIPE	detflg##	;detached?
	 JRST	toutp9		;yes, we can't flush!
	MOVEI	t,oficha	;<KPJ.235> output channel
	DEVTYP	t,		;<KPJ.235> get physical properties
	 JRST	toutp0		;<KPJ.235> "should never take the error return"
	JUMPE	t,toutp0	;<KPJ.235> channel unassigned
	ANDI	t,TY.DEV	;<KPJ.235> extract device code
	CAIN	t,.TYTTY	;<KPJ.235> terminal?
	 CALL	foutpu##	;<KPJ.235> yes, dump the terminal buffer
toutp0:	OUT	ttycha,		;<KPJ.235> force out the TTY: buffer
	 JRST	toutp9		;ok, return if done
	SETZ	t,		;sleep forever, we'll be interrupted
	HIBER	t,		;go to sleep
	 error	<toutpu monito>	;should not happen
	JRST	toutpu		;go and retry now
>;T10
T20,<	$Setz	1,.CHNUL		; finish the buffer with a null
	IDPB	1,ottbuf##+.BFPTR
	HRROI	1,ttobuf##
	PSOUT%				; print buffer
	MOVEI	t,8*^O23*5-1		; max number of chars in buffer
	MOVEM	t,ottbuf##+.BFCTR
	MOVE	t,[POINT 7,ttobuf##]	; pointer to buffer
	MOVEM	t,ottbuf##+.BFPTR
>;T20
toutp9:	return





;+
;TGET		get a character from terminal input buffer,
;		ignoring multiple LFs
;accepts	HAVENQ/	=0 if no ENQ wait in progress
;			#0 if ENQ wait in progress
;		PASFLG/	=0  if not reading a password
;			=1  reading password, already output prompter
;			=-1 reading password, output prompter first
;		LFIFLG/	=0 last character not LF
;			#0 previous character LF
;returns	CH/	character
;-

tget::	save	<gp1,nr>
	$Setz	ch,			;<KPJ.245!KPJ.151> ho hum...
tget1:
IFN	ftphon,<			;<KPJ.163> if text phone support...
	SKIPE	pasflg##		;<BCQ> reading a password?
	 JRST[
T10,<		SKIPE	havenq##	;<TEQ> can't accept waiting for TTY
					;<TEQ> I/O if owning an interlock
		 JRST[	error	<tget monito>]
>;T10
		MOVE	t,pasflg##	;<BCQ> get the flag
		CAMN	t,[-1]		;<KPJ.164!BCQ> this is first time?
		 CALL	askque##	;[BCQ] yes, so ask him
		CALL	toutpu		;[BCQ] and force out the buffer
		MOVEI	t,1
		MOVEM	t,pasflg##	;<BCQ> indicate we've read read a char
T10,<		INCHRW	ch>		;[BCQ] read a character
T20,<		PBIN%			;[BCQ] read a character
		MOVE	ch,1		;[BCQ] and get into ch
				;[BCQ] char will be backed over at STRCON
>;T20
		JRST	tget7]		;[BCQ] return the character
>;ftphon
tget0:	SOSL	ittbuf##+.BFCTR			;<KPJ.241> any characters?
	 JRST[	ILDB	ch,ittbuf##+.BFPTR	;<KPJ.241> yes, get one
		JRST	tget7]			;<KPJ.241> character got
	CALL	toutpu			;output terminal buffer
	CALL	ospclr			;<KPJ.102!BDQ> clear ^O bit here
	MOVE	t,lfiflg##		;<KPJ.164> get LF flag
	CAME	t,[-2]			;<KPJ.164> ignoring multiple LFs?
	 CALL	askque##		;<KPJ.102> no, ask question
tget6:	CALL	ttinp			;<KPJ.151> read input from terminal
	 JRST	tget1			;<KPJ.151> OK, we got some stuff
	SETZM	linpos##		;<KPJ.151> ^Z was typed, indicate EOF
	CALL	eoltty##		;<KPJ.151> newline hacking
T10,<	JRST	tget6>		;<KPJ.161!KPJ.153!KPJ.151> get that char, now
T20,<	JRST	tget0>			;<KPJ.241> get character, now

tget7:	JUMPE	ch,tget1		;ignore NULs
	SKIPE	lfiflg##		;[KPJ.33,34] last char line feed ?
	 JRST[	CAIE	ch,.CHLFD	;[KPJ.33,34] yes, LF ?
		 JRST	.+1		;<KPJ.164> no
		MOVNI	t,2		;<KPJ.164> yes, set ignore LF "ON"
		MOVEM	t,lfiflg##	;<KPJ.164> . . .
		JRST	tget1]		;<KPJ.163,33,34> go for next character
	return

	
;+
T10,<					;<KPJ.151>
;MICTTY		see if MIC state changed
;returns	+1	yes, has changed
;		+2	no, has not changed

mictty:	MOVEI	t2,.TOGMS		;[KPJ.35] read MIC status data
	SETO	t3,			;[KPJ.35] controlling tty
	MOVE	t,[%CNVER]		;<KPJ.240> get T10 version
	GETTAB	t,			;<KPJ.240> . . .
	 error	<mictty-1 monito>	;<KPJ.240> kapow!
	CAIL	t,^O70300		;<KPJ.240> 7.03 or later?
	 JRST	mictt3			;<KPJ.240> yes, use new method
;
;This code worked before 7.03
;
	MOVE	t,[2,,t2]		;[KPJ.35] len,,addr
	TRMOP.	t,			;read MIC status
	 JRST	mictt4			;failed, not a MIC session
	JRST	mictt5			;success, a MIC session
;
;This code works with with 7.03 (but NOT according to the documentation)
;
mictt3:	MOVE	t,[3,,t2]		;<KPJ.240!KPJ.236> len,,addr
	TRMOP.	t,			;<KPJ.240> 
	 CALL[	CAME	t,@mictt3	;<KPJ.240!KPJ.237> any error code?
		 error	<mictty-2 monito> ;<KPJ.240> yes, die
		$setz	t4,		;<KPJ.245!KPJ.237> no, simulate a "no"
		RET]			;<KPJ.237>
	JUMPN	t4,mictt5		;<KPJ.236!KPJ.240> not a MIC session?
	Fall	mictt4			;<KPJ.240> a MIC session
;
;Not a MIC session at the moment.
;
mictt4:	SKIPN	micflg##		;<KPJ.240> no, MIC session before?
	 JRST	mictt8			;no, so continue
	SETZB	t,micflg##		;clear MIC flag
	JRST	mictt1
;
;A MIC session at the moment.

mictt5:	SKIPE	micflg##		;<KPJ.240> MIC session before too?
	 JRST	mictt8

	SETOB	t,micflg##		;no, so we must reopen TTY
mictt1:	CLOSE	ttycha,			;<KPJ.151> close TTY channel
	MOVSI	t2,(UU.AIO)		;<KPJ.151> non-blocking I/O
	CAIN	t,0			;<KPJ.151>
	 IORM	t2,opntty##+.OPMOD	;<KPJ.151>
	CAIE	t,0			;<KPJ.151>
	 ANDCAM	t2,opntty##+.OPMOD	;<KPJ.151>
	CALL	eoftty			;<KPJ.151> and re-OPEN TTY
	TRNA
mictt8:	 Skpret
	return
>;T10



;+
T10,<					;<KPJ.151>
;MICP		test for MIC-in-progress
;returns	+1	yes, a MIC session
;		+2	no, no MIC session
;-

micp:	MOVEI	t2,.TOGMS		;[KPJ.35] read MIC status data
	SETO	t3,			;[KPJ.35] controlling tty
	MOVE	t,[2,,t2]		;[KPJ.35] len,,addr
	TRMOP.	t,			;read MIC status
	 $Skipa				;not a MIC session
	  skpret
	return
>;T10



;+
;TTINP		read a line from the terminal
;	T10:		read from TTY:
;	T20:		do a TEXTI to read from primary input
;accepts	HAVENQ/	=0 have not an ENQ interlock
;			#0 have an ENQ interlock
;		MICFLG/	=0 no a MIC in progress
;			#0 a MIC in progress
;returns	+1 got a line
;		+2 ^Z
;-

ttinp:	CALL	toutpu
T10,<	SKIPE	havenq##		;<KPJ.151!TEQ> can't accept TTY wait
	 error	<ttinp monito>		;<KPJ.151!TEQ> if owning an interlock

ttin1:	CALL	mictty			;<KPJ.151> MIC status changed?
	 JRST	ttin1			;<KPJ.151> yes, re-open TTY accordingly
	IN	ttycha,			;get the buffer
	 SKIPG	ittbuf##+.BFCTR		;<KPJ.112> got anything in buffer?
	  $Skipa			;<KPJ.112> no
	   JRST	ttin9			;<KPJ.151> OK, we've got a buffer
	STATZ	ttycha,IO.EOF		;test if end of file (^Z)
	 JRST[	CALL	reitty		;<KPJ.151> yes, re-initialize TTY
		skpret			;<KPJ.151> +2 return
		JRST	ttin9]		;<KPJ.151> return

	MOVEI	t,inslp1		;[KPJ.37] use t as HIBER counter
	SKIPN	logflg##		;[BCQ] are we LOGGED IN?
	 MOVEI	t,inslp2		;[KPJ.37!BCQ] if we aren't logged in,
					;[BCQ] there is a much shorter timeout
ttin2:	MOVEI	gp1,^D60*^D1000		;a minute in sleep-time
	CALL	sleept			;fall asleep while waiting
	 JRST	ttin1			;<KPJ.151> read the line from TTY
	MOVE	gp1,selffl##		;<KPJ.61> get my flags
	Txne	gp1,idlpfl		;<KPJ.61> idle killer active?
	 JRST	ttin2			;<KPJ.61!51> no, loop
	SOJGE	t,ttin2			;<KPJ.61> yes, try again

					;<KPJ.151> terminal timeout

	MOVEI	t2,.TORMT		;[KPJ.35] get "remote" bit
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
IFN	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	nr,[2,,trmblk##]	;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;t3<>t2+1
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<			;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	nr,<2,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;t3=t2+1
	TRMOP.	nr,			;<KPJ.35>
	 warn	<monito tget trmop read tormt> ;<KPJ.41>

	JUMPE	nr,ttin9		;no remote terminal ?
	JRST	endkom##		;go and finish up, we'll be killed
ttin9:
>;T10

T20,<	MOVE	1,txtarg##+.RDBFP	;pointer to start of buffer
	MOVEM	1,txtarg##+.RDDBP	;should be initialized here
	MOVEI	1,8*<<^D80/5>+3>*5-1	;size of text buffer
	MOVEM	1,txtarg##+.RDDBC
ttinp1:	MOVEI	1,txtarg##
ttinp0:	TEXTI%				;<KPJ.245> read string from TTY
	 error	<ttinp monito>
	LDB	1,txtarg##+.RDDBP	;yes, get break char
	CAIN	1,.CHBSP		;[KPJ.11][BDQ] was last char a ^H?
	 JRST[	MOVE	1,txtarg##+.RDDBP	;[BDQ] yes, zap byte pointer
		Decrbp	1			;<KPJ.177> decrement byte ptr
		Decrbp	1			;<KPJ.177>
		MOVEI	2,0(1)
		CAIGE	2,ttibuf##		;[BDQ] check if outside buffer
		 JRST	ttinp
		MOVEM	1,txtarg##+.RDDBP	;[BDQ] store byte pointer
		AOS	txtarg##+.RDDBC		;[BDQ] zap byte count
		AOS	txtarg##+.RDDBC
		JRST	ttinp1]

	CAIE	1,.CHSPC		;[KPJ.11] was last char a space?
	 JRST	ttinp2			;no, don't try an ACR
	MOVEI	1,.PRIIN
	RFPOS%				;where on the screen are we?
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ouch
	HRRZ	2,2			;only column, thank you
	CAIG	2,irmarg		;beyond margin?
	 JRST	ttinp1			;no
	HRROI	1,[BYTE (7) .CHCRT,.CHLFD,.CHNUL]
	PSOUT%				;<KPJ.245!KPJ.41> yes, "echo" it
	MOVEI	1,.CHCRT		;<KPJ.11> transform the space into CR..
	DPB	1,txtarg##+.RDDBP
	MOVEI	1,.CHLFD		;<KPJ.11> ..followed by LF
	IDPB	1,txtarg##+.RDDBP
	SOS	txtarg##+.RDDBC		;decrement byte count also
ttinp2:	MOVEI	3,8*^O23*5-1		;max space in buffer
	SUB	3,txtarg##+.RDDBC	;calculate # of chars read
	MOVEM	3,ittbuf##+.BFCTR	;<KPJ.201> store that
	MOVE	3,[POINT 7,ttibuf##]	;pointer to input buffer
	MOVEM	3,ittbuf##+.BFPTR	;<KPJ.201> store that too
	MOVE	3,[POINT 7,rtybuf##,6]	;reset..
	MOVEM	3,rtypnt##		;..the bytepointer
	$Setz	3,.CHNUL		;<KPJ.245> make ASCIZ
	DPB	3,rtypnt##
	CAIN	1,.CHCNZ		;[KPJ.11]!KPJ.26 was last char ^Z?
	 JRST[	HRROI	1,[BYTE (7) .CHCRT,.CHLFD,.CHNUL]
					;yes, echo CRLF after "^Z"
		PSOUT%
		skpret			;<KPJ.126> and give +2 return
		JRST	.+1]
>;T20
	return


;+
;EOFTTY		end of file on terminal (Tops-10 only)
T10,<
;-

eoftty:	CALL	reitty			; at EOF, reopen TTY channel
	SETZM	linpos##		; clear line position
	branch	eoltty##		; new line handling
>;T10

;+
;ECHOFF		set echo off	(Tops-10 version)
;-

echoff::
T10,<	SKIPE	echflg##	;echo ?
	 JRST	echof1		;yes
	MOVE	t,selffl##	;[KPJ.31] get personal flags
	Txne	t,lfepfl	;[KPJ.31] LINE FEED ECHO?
echof1:	 CALL	seecof		;[KPJ.31] yes, turn off echo
	return
>;T10
T20,<	Fall	seecof>			;[KPJ.31] fall into SEECOF routine



;+
;SEECOF		set echo off
;-

seecof::
T10,<	GETSTS	ttycha,t		; get old TTY status
	TRO	t,IO.SUP		; include no echo bit
	SETSTS	ttycha,(t)		; turn off echoing
	CALL	toutpu			; output terminal
>;T10
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT
	RFMOD%				; get mode word
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	TRZ	2,TT%ECO		; clear echo bit
	SFMOD%				; set mode word
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
>;T20
	return



;+
;ECHON		set echo on
;-

echon::
T10,<	SKIPE	echflg##	;echo?
	 JRST	echon1		;yes
	MOVE	t,selffl##	;[KPJ.31] get personal flags
	Txnn	t,lfepfl	;[KPJ.31] LINE FEED ECHO?
	 JRST	echon9		; no
echon1:	GETSTS	ttycha,t	; get status of TTY channel
	TRZ	t,IO.SUP	; include suppress status
	SETSTS	ttycha,(t)	; turn on echoing
	CALL	toutpu		; output terminal
echon9:
>;T10
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT
	RFMOD%				;get JFN mode word
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> argh
	TRO	2,TT%ECO		;set echo bit
	SFMOD%				;set JFN mode word
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ugh
>;T20
	return






;+
;CLEAR		clear input
;returns	CHPT/	pointing to a NUL
;-

clear::	save	<bp>
	MOVE	bp,[POINT 7,[0]]	;zap byte pointer
	MOVEM	bp,chpt##		;save it
T10,<	CLRBFI>				; clear input buffer
T20,<	MOVEI	1,.PRIIN
	CFIBF%				; clear input buffer
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
>;T20
	MOVEI	t,terpro##		;<KPJ.154> get terminal producer
	MOVEM	t,produc##		;<KPJ.154>
	SETZM	tmpflg##		;<KPJ.154>
	return





;+
;GUDATE		get "universal" (Tops-10) daytime
;returns	GP1/	date
;		CURDAT/	date
;-

gudate::
T10,<	MOVE	gp1,[%CNDTM]		;[KPJ.35] get universal daytime
	GETTAB	gp1,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito gudate gettab cndtm> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	save	<1,2,3,4>
	MOVEI	1,.SFTMZ		;get timezone (hours west of Greenwich)
	TMON%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	MOVE	gp1,2			; save timezone
	GTAD%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	MOVE	2,1			; set up args for ODCNV%
	SETZ	4,
	ODCNV%				; find out what conversions are used.
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	TLNE	4,(IC%ADS)		; test if daylight saving time is on
	 SUBI	gp1,1			;shift 1h to the east if it is on
	IMUL	gp1,[-1B1/^D24]		; multiply timezone with -2^34/24.
	ASH	gp1,-^D16		;div with 2^16 to get fraction of day
	ADD	gp1,1			; make the "local" UDT that KOM wants
>;T20
	MOVEM	gp1,curdat##		;save current date
	return





;+
;GLYEAR		get local year
;returns	NR/	year#
;-

glyear::
T10,<	MOVE	nr,[%CNYER]		;[KPJ.35] get local year
	GETTAB	nr,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito glyear gettab cnyer> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	SETO	2,
	SETZ	4,
	ODCNV%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	HLRZ	nr,2
>;T20
	return





;+
;GLMONT		get local month
;returns	NR/	month# (1..12)
;-

glmont::
T10,<	MOVE	nr,[%CNMON]		;[KPJ.35] get local month
	GETTAB	nr,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito glmont gettab cnmon> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	SETO	2,
	SETZ	4,
	ODCNV%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	HRRZI	nr,1(2)			;On Twenex, first month is #0
>;T20
	return


;+
;GLDAY		get local day of week
;returns	NR/	day#	(1..7)
;-

glday::
T10,<	MOVE	nr,[%CNDAY]		;[KPJ.35] get local day
	GETTAB	nr,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito glday gettab cnday> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	SETO	2,
	SETZ	4,
	ODCNV%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	HLRZ	nr,3
	ADDI	nr,1			;On Twenex, Monday is day #0
>;T20
	return


;+
;ALLOCM		allocate enough memory
;accepts	FREE/	wanted memory
;		.JBREL/	RH: highest used memory address
;returns	+1 failure:
;			T10: with T/ CORE error code
;			T20: memory is write-protected or invalid
;-

allocm::HRRZ	t,.JBREL	;get end of memory
	CAML	t,free		;<KPJ.174> already that much free ?
	 JRST	alloc8		;<KPJ.174> yep
	CALL	foallo		;no, force allocation
	 $Skipa			;<KPJ.174> failed
alloc8:	  skpret		;<KPJ.174> +2 return means success
alloc9:	return			;<KPJ.174>


;+
;FOALLO		force allocation
;accepts	FREE/	memory end
;returns	+1	failure:
;			T10:	with T/	CORE error code
;			T20:	memory full
;		+2	success, with .JBFF/	new memory size
;-

foallo::MOVE	t,free			;get end
	ADDI	t,fresiz		;get more
					;<SEE>dont shrink, would mung cell area
T10,<	HRRZ	t2,.JBREL		;<KPJ.204>
	CAMLE	t,t2			;<KPJ.204!SEE> shrinking memory use?
	 JRST[	CORE	t,		;no, get more memory
		 JRST 	foall8		;<KPJ.174> can't, tell user about this
		JRST	.+1]		;<KPJ.174> OK
>;T10
T20,<
;You could use RPACS% JSYS to test for page accessibility, but that's a lot of
;useless overhead, since this routine is called every now and then.  We just
;need to test if page is write-protected, which we barf on.  We don't want to
;destroy any data, so we use a page fault call to test for page accessability,
;since that is well optimized on Twenex.

	MOVE	t2,0(t)		;<KPJ.174> get old stuff
	MOVEM	t2,0(t)		;<KPJ.174> put it back
	ERJMP	foall8		;<KPJ.174> fails if write-protected
>;T20
	MOVEM	t,.JBFF		;<KPJ.174> set new lowseg end
	skpret			;<KPJ.174> +2 return means success
	JRST	foall9		;<KPJ.174>

foall8:	PUSH	P,str		;<KPJ.174> save precious data
	MOVEI	str,zfoall##	;<KPJ.174> "arrggh... I lost my memory"
	CALL	errmsg##	;<KPJ.174> that's an error
	SETOM	errfl##		;<KPJ.174> make random routines give up
	SETOM	intflg##	;<KPJ.174> make random routines give up	
	POP	P,str		;<KPJ.174> restore garbage
foall9:	return			;<KPJ.174>


;+
;RELTTY		release terminal
;-

reltty::
T10,<	MOVEI	t2,.TONFC+.TOSET	;[KPJ.35] change "CR/LF bit"
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
	MOVE	t4,trmnfc##		;[KPJ.35] restore TTY CRLF setting
	MOVE	t,[3,,t2]		;[KPJ.35] len,,addr
	TRMOP.	t,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito reltty trmop write tonfc> ;[KPJ.41]

	MOVEI	t2,.TOACR+.TOSET	;[KPJ.35] change ACR flag
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
	MOVE	t4,trmcr##		;[KPJ.35] restore ACR setting
	MOVE	t,[3,,t2]		;[KPJ.35] len,,addr
	TRMOP.	t,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito reltty trmop write toacr> ;[KPJ.41]

	MOVEI	t2,.TOLCT+.TOSET	;[KPJ.35] change LC flag
	MOVE	t3,uxxtrm##		;<KPJ.35> this UDX
	MOVE	t4,trmlct##		;[KPJ.35] restore lower case setting
	MOVE	t,[3,,t2]		;[KPJ.35] len,,addr
	TRMOP.	t,			;[KPJ.35]
	 warn	<monito reltty trmop write tolct> ;[KPJ.41]

	SKIPN	detflg##		;detached?
	 RELEAS	ttycha,			;no, release terminal

	.foo==0
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<IFE	<t4-t3-1>,<.foo==1>>
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	.bar==ftcpu			;<KPJ.245> remember old FTCPU
	ftcpu==.pdpx			;<KPJ.245> make believe we are not KL10
>;can't use ACs
KL10,<	DMOVE	t2,[EXP .TOSET+.TOPSZ,-1]> ;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> change "PAGE nn"
KL10N,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOSET+.TOPSZ	;[KPJ.35] change "PAGE nnn"
	SETO	t3,			;[KPJ.35] controlling terminal
>;KL10N
	MOVE	t4,oldpag##		;<KPJ.135!KPJ.35> "TTY PAGE nnn"
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	ftcpu==.bar			;<KPJ.245> restore old FTCPU
	PURGE	.bar			;<KPJ.245> forget this trickery
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. argblk
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEM	t4,trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	MOVE	t,[3,,t2]		;[KPJ.35] len,,addr
>;can use ACs
	PURGE	.foo			;<KPJ.245> forget this fiddling
	TRMOP.	t,			;[BCQ] restore paged mode
	 warn	<monito reltty trmop write topsz> ;[KPJ.41]
	
	.foo==0
IFE	<t3-t2-1>,<IFE	<t4-t3-1>,<.foo==1>>
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	.bar==ftcpu			;<KPJ.245> remember old CPU type
	ftcpu==.pdpx			;<KPJ.245> fake a no-KL10
>;can't use ACs
KL10,<	DMOVE	t2,[EXP .TOSET+.TOLNB,-1]> ;<KPJ.245!KPJ.35> change "LENGTH n"
KL10N,<	MOVEI	t2,.TOSET+.TOLNB	;[KPJ.35] change "LENGTH nnn"
	SETO	t3,			;[KPJ.35] controlling terminal
>;KL10N
	MOVE	t4,oldpsz##		;<KPJ.135!KPJ.35> "TTY LENGTH nnn"
IFE	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can't use ACs
	ftcpu==.bar			;<KPJ.245> put back reality
	PURGE	.bar			;<KPJ.245> forget this trickery
	MOVEM	t2,trmblk##+0		;<KPJ.245> save in TRMOP. block
	MOVEM	t3,trmblk##+1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEM	t4,trmblk##+2		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	t,[3,,trmblk##]		;<KPJ.245> len,,addr
>;can't use ACs
IFN	.foo,<				;<KPJ.245> can use ACs
	$Movx	t,<3,,t2>		;<KPJ.246!KPJ.35> len,,addr
>;can use ACs
	TRMOP.	t,			;<BCQ> restore paged mode
	 warn	<monito reltty trmop write topsz> ;[KPJ.41]
>;T10
T20,<	CALL	toutpu
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT
	MOVE	2,oldmod##
	SFMOD%				; restore parameters
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	STPAR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVEI	2,.MOXOF		;[BDQ] restore pause end-page setting
	MOVE	3,oldpag##		;<KPJ.135>
	MTOPR%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	$Dmove	2,oldcoc##		;<KPJ.245> restore CCOC words
	SFCOC%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245>
	MOVEI	1,.FHJOB		;[BDQ] restore terminal interrupt word
	MOVE	2,oldtiw##
	STIW%
	 ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245!KPJ.131!BDQ> ugh
>;T20
	return


;+
;DISCIN		disable ^C interrupt
;-

discin::save	<t>
T10,<	MOVE	t,[PS.FCS!PS.FRC!stpcon]
	PISYS.	t,			;remove ^C PSI condition
	 error	<discin monito>
>;T10
T20,<	$Dmovi	1,.FHSLF,<1B<cc.chn>>	;<KPJ.246>
	DIC%				;deactivate ^C-channel
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPj.246>
>;T20
	return


;+
;ENACIN		enable ^C interrupt
;-

enacin::
T10,<	MOVE	t,[PS.FAC!PS.FON!stpcon]
	PISYS.	t,			;turn CTRL/C trap on
	 error	<enacin monito>
>;T10
T20,<	$Dmovi	1,.FHSLF,<1B<cc.chn>>	;<KPJ.246>
	AIC%				;activate ^C-channel
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
>;T20
	return



;+
T20,<
;TRPSTP		^C interrupt routine
;-

trpstp::SKIPE	havenq##		;<KPJ.46> have ENQ on database?
	 JRST[	PUSH	P,1		;<KPj.245> no, save AC 1
		HRROI	1,[BYTE (7) "^","C",.CHNUL] ;<KPJ.246> "echo" CTRL/C
		PSOUT%			;<KPJ.245> . . .
		POP	P,1		;<KPJ.245> . . .
		DEBRK%			;<KPJ.245> bye, bye
		ERCAL	fatal##]	;<KPJ.245> ugh
	PUSH	P,1			;<KPJ.245> dis-trustful code
	PUSH	P,2			;<KPJ.245> . . .
	PUSH	P,3			;<KPJ.245> . . .
	PUSH	P,4			;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;<KPJ.245> clear output buffer
	CFOBF%				;<KPJ.245> . . .
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ouch
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;<KPJ.245> get JFN mode word
	RFMOD%				;<KPJ.245> . . .
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ouch
	TLZE	2,(TT%OSP)		;<KPJ.245> clear suppress-output bit
	 SFMOD%				;<KPJ.245> . . .
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ugh
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;<BDQ> get CCOC words
	RFCOC%				;<BDQ> . . .
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ugh

;<BDQ> trick: see if CCOC of CTRL/_ has changed, means we were DETACHed

	LDB	1,[POINT 2,3,2*<"_"-"@">-^D36+1]
	CAIN	1,.CCSIM		;changed from SIMULATE?
	 JRST[				;<KPJ.245> no, this is for *real*
		HRROI	1,[BYTE (7) "^","C",.CHCRT,.CHLFD,.CHNUL]
		PSOUT%			;<KPJ.245> "echo" the CTRL/C
		SETZM	linpos##	;we are now at left margin
		SETOM	stpflg##	;<BDQ> ^C flag
		MOVE	1,[PC%USR!endkom##] ;<KPJ.245>
		MOVEM	1,lev1pc##	;<KPJ.245> user mode, return to ENDKOM
		JRST	trpst9]		;<KPJ.245> exit CTRL/C handler

;We come here after being DETACHed and then reATTACHed
;<BDQ> no ^C exit if caused by ATTACH

	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT
	TRO	3,<.CCSIM>B<2*<"_"-"@">-^D36+1>	;<KPJ.245> put back SIMULATE
	SFCOC%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ouch
	HRROI	1,zzctlc##		;<KPJ.245> hello there
	PSOUT%				;<KPJ.245>
	HRRZ	1,lev1pc##		;<BDQ> get interrupted PC
	CAIE	1,ttinp0+1		;<KPJ.245!BDQ> was it in TEXTI% jsys?
	 JRST	trpst9			;<BDQ> no, exit
	MOVE	1,[PC%USR!ttinp]	;<KPJ.245!BDQ> user mode, go to TTINP
	MOVEM	1,lev1pc##		;<BDQ> "return" to TTINP

;Come here to restore I/O world after ATTACH.

	MOVEI	1,.PRIIN		;<BDQ>
	CFIBF%				;<BDQ> clear input buffer
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ouch
					;<KPJ.245> restore buffer ring
	SETZM	ittbuf##+.BFADR		;<KPJ.245> clear buffer ring
	SETZM	ittbuf##+.BFPTR		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	SETZM	ittbuf##+.BFCTR		;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEI	1,noftto*^O23*5-1	;<KPJ.245> max #characters in buffer
	MOVEM	1,ottbuf##+.BFCTR	;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVE	1,[POINT 7,ttobuf##]	;<KPJ.245> buffer byte pointer
	MOVEM	1,ottbuf##+.BFPTR	;<KPJ.245> . . .
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;<KPJ.245>
	RFMOD%				;<KPJ.245> get JFN mode word
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> argh
	TRO	2,TT%ECO		;<KPJ.245> set echo bit
	SFMOD%				;<KPJ.245> set JFN mode word
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> ugh
	HRROI	1,rtybuf##		;simulate CTRL/R
	PSOUT%				;. . .

trpst9:	POP	P,4			;<KPJ.245!KPJ.46> restore stack
	POP	P,3			;<KPJ.245> . . .
	POP	P,2			;<KPJ.245> . . .
	POP	P,1			;<KPJ.245> . . .
	DEBRK%				;return somewhere
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.245> grunt

;+
;CAINT	^A interrupt routine (not documented)
;-

caint:	save	<1,2,3>
	MOVEI	1,.PRIIN
	RFPOS%				;where on the screen are we?
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	HRRZ	2,2			;only column, thank you
	JUMPE	2,cain1
	HRROI	1,[BYTE (7) .CHCRT,.CHLFD,.CHNUL] ;<KPJ.246>
	PSOUT%				;<KPJ.246>
cain1:	$Dmovi	1,.PRIOUT,.CHSPC	;<KPJ.246> output one space
	BOUT%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	$Dmovi	2,<-1>,<OT%NDA!OT%SCL>	;<KPJ.246>
	ODTIM%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	MOVEI	2,.CHSPC		;space
	BOUT%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	CALL	komsts
	rstreg				;<ZOT.250>
	DEBRK%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
>;T20

;+
T20,<
;KOMSTS		routine to output a CTRL/A status message.

;			*NOTE*
;			 ====
;		May only use ACs 1, 2, 3, 4 freely.
;		May use P as a stack pointer only.
;		All other ACs *must* be preserved. 
;-

komsts:	GETNM%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	SKIPN	2,1			;<KPJ.45> zero name?
	 MOVE	2,[SIXBIT !(priv)!]	;<KPJ.45> make the default one

komst1:	$Setz	1,			;<KPJ.246> output SIXBIT name
	LSHC	1,6
	ADDI	1,"A"-'A'		;make ASCIZ
	PBOUT%
	ERCAL	fatal
	JUMPN	2,komst1

	MOVEI	1,.CHSPC		;output space
	PBOUT%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>

	HRRZ	1,lev2pc##		;interrupted from where?
	MOVEI	2,ststab		;<KPJ.142> point at wait table
stslup:	MOVE	3,0(2)			;<KPJ.142> get wait state
	JUMPE	3,[			;<KPJ.142> not a known wait state
		MOVE	2,lev2pc##	;<KPJ.142> get interrupted PC
		HRRO	1,ststab-2	;<KPJ.142> assume we are in RN state
		TLNN	2,(PC%USR)	;<KPJ.124> executing a JSYS?
		 HRRO	1,ststab-1	;<KPJ.124> yes
		JRST	stsout]		;<KPJ.142>
	CAME	1,3			;<KPJ.142> this wait state?
	 JRST[	ADDI	2,2		;<KPJ.142> no, step forward
		JRST	stslup]		;<KPJ.142> try next
	HRRO	1,1(2)			;<KPJ.142> get wait state text
stsout:	PSOUT%
	ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
	JUMPE	3,[			;<KPJ.145> random state?
		TLNE	2,(PC%USR)	;<KPJ.145> yes, JSYS?
		 JRST	.+1		;<KPJ.145> no, forget this
		MOVEI	1,.CHSPC	;<KPJ.145>
		PBOUT%			;<KPJ.145>
		ERCAL	fatal##		;<KPJ.246>
		MOVEI	1,.CHLPR	;<KPJ.145> yes, output left paren
		PBOUT%			;<KPJ.145>
		ERCAL	fatal##		;<KPJ.246>
		HRRZ	2,lev2pc##	;<KPJ.150> here we are again...
		SUBI	2,1		;<KPJ.150> this is more like it...
		HRRZ	2,@2		;<KPJ.150> get JSYS#
		HRRZ	1,jstab(2)	;<KPJ.165!KPJ.150> any name for it?
		SKIPN	@1		;<KPJ.165> anything there?
		 JRST[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !JSYS !]	;<KPJ.165> no, JSYS nnn
			PSOUT%				;<KPJ.165>
			ERCAL	fatal##			;<KPJ.246>
			MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;<KPJ.165>
			MOVEI	3,<FLD(8,NO%RDX)>	;<KPJ.165>
			NOUT%				;<KPJ.165>
			 ERJMP[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !???!]	;<KPJ.165>
				PSOUT%			;<KPJ.165>
				JRST	.+1]		;<KPJ.165>
			JRST	.+1]			;<KPJ.165>
		PSOUT%			;<KPJ.150> output name
		MOVEI	1,.CHRPR	;<KPJ.145> output closing paren
		PBOUT%			;<KPJ.145>
		JRST	.+1]		;<KPJ.145>
	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !, PC=!]	;<KPJ.142>
	PSOUT%				;<KPJ.142>
	MOVEI	1,.PRIOUT		;<KPJ.142> no
	HRRZ	2,lev2pc##		;<KPJ.142> get PC
	MOVEI	3,<FLD(8,NO%RDX)>	;<KPJ.142> octal
	NOUT%				;<KPJ.142> output PC
	 ERJMP[	HRROI	1,[ASCIZ !???!]	;<KPJ.142> failed
		PSOUT%			;<KPJ.142> say so
		JRST	.+1]		;<KPJ.142>
stsxit:	Tmsg	<.
>
	return

